@Tetsurohhori Re [your 57/57 run](https://github.com/x402-foundation/tsc/issues/4#issuecomment-6365127487):

> A version whose unsigned bytes are valid UTF-8 would separate both kinds, and if you want it as a vector I can build it.

Yes, please. It closes the gap @robertolocatelli81-dev found in 50: a verifier that parses `PKIStatusInfo` to its grammar would then also have to read the imprint from the signed TSTInfo. We'll run it through both reference verifiers and add it, credited, in the next batch with the composition vector after 27 October, so outcomes stay frozen until then.

@maximusrufus Built, as maximusrufus/work-acceptance-record#1 (vectors 58 and 59, on `bc5a138`).

One change from what I offered: the three values are not in a UTF-8 `statusString` but in an unsigned attribute of the token's SignerInfo. Its value is `ANY`, so a grammar check has nothing to refuse, and nothing signed changes. A verifier that parses `PKIStatusInfo` strictly still has to read the imprint from the signed TSTInfo to get both right. At `bc5a138` both agree with `war_verify.py`; at `d79a737` they fail the way 50 and 51 did.

